Feature: A failed push records why it failed

  push-sweep's failure record carries only an attempt count today, so a long
  failure streak cannot be diagnosed. The underlying git error must travel
  with it, on one line, and reach the operator alarm too.

  Background:
    Given a repository whose push sweep is configured against a remote

  # BL-903 push-sweep-discards-failure-reason-01
  Scenario Outline: A push failure records the underlying reason
    Given the remote will reject a push because <cause>
    When the push sweep attempts a push
    Then the failure record carries the attempt count
    And the failure record carries a recognisable fragment of the git error

    Examples:
      | cause                        |
      | the push is not a fast-forward |
      | the remote URL is unreachable  |

  # BL-903 push-sweep-discards-failure-reason-02
  Scenario: Two different causes produce two distinguishable records
    Given the remote will reject a push because the push is not a fast-forward
    When the push sweep attempts a push
    And the remote will reject a push because the remote URL is unreachable
    And the push sweep attempts a push
    Then the two failure records differ in their recorded reason

  # BL-903 push-sweep-discards-failure-reason-03
  Scenario: A multi-line git error still occupies one record
    Given the remote will reject a push with a multi-line error
    When the push sweep attempts a push
    Then exactly one new record is written

  # BL-903 push-sweep-discards-failure-reason-04
  Scenario: The operator alarm names the reason, not only the count
    Given the remote will reject a push because the remote URL is unreachable
    When the push sweep has failed enough times to arm the alarm
    Then the alarm body carries the recorded reason

  # BL-903 push-sweep-discards-failure-reason-05
  Scenario: A successful push writes no failure record
    Given the remote will accept a push
    When the push sweep attempts a push
    Then no failure record is written
    And the recorded attempt count is reset to zero

  # BL-903 push-sweep-discards-failure-reason-06
  Scenario: Retry timing is unchanged
    Given the remote will reject a push because the remote URL is unreachable
    When the push sweep attempts a push
    Then the next attempt becomes due after the same backoff as before this change
